SUMMARY:Kissing the Veil: The Art of Biblical Translation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T203000
UID:tribe-10004490@nertamid.org
DESCRIPTION:Hayim Nahman Bialik\, Israel’s national poet\, once compared
  reading the Bible in translation to kissing your bride through a veil. Co
 ming from him\, that’s an understandable view. But for those of us who a
 ren’t native Hebrew speakers\, translation isn’t a barrier between us 
 and our most sacred texts — it’s our entryway to them. And honestly\, 
 once you know what that veil is doing\, a kiss doesn’t sound so bad. Tra
 nslation is an art form\, and every translated text a work of art in its o
 wn right\, full 
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/kissing-the-veil-the-art-of-biblical-transl
 ation/2026-12-14/
X-SOURCE:Temple Ner Tamid
END:VEVENT
